+---
+
+## 1. Connection, auth and shared conventions
+
+- **Paths:** endpoints live under the shared app root, e.g.
+  `{APP_URL}/modules/learning/api/inbound/receive-turnover-risk.php`.
+  Inside the app, build the base with `includes/app-base.php`:
+  `AppBase::urlFor('modules/learning/api/inbound/receive-turnover-risk.php')`.
+  In CLI/cron there is no request, so `AppBase::url()` returns `""` — set a `LD_BASE_URL`
+  environment variable (or a constant in your module) for scheduled jobs.
+- **Transport:** JSON body, `POST` for the receive endpoints, `GET` for the pulls.
+- **Identity:** L&D's `learner_id` === `em_employees.employee_id`. Your `employee_id` is the same value.
+- **Logging:** every call you make lands in `ld_integration_log` (`direction`, `module_name`, `endpoint`,
+  `status`, `payload`, `error_message`) — that is the first place to look when a push "didn't work".
+
+### Keys — read this before you write the caller
+
+| Direction | Endpoint | `X-API-Key` that validates today |
+|---|---|---|
+| Push (1–4) | `api/inbound/receive-*` | **`wa_…`** (module `workforce-analytics`) |
+| Read-back (6) | `api/outbound/get-workforce-integration-status.php` | **`wa_…`** (same key) |
+| Pull (5) | `api/outbound/get-workforce-analytics.php` | **`ld_…`** (module `learning-development`) ⚠️ |
+
+Your key pair, from `ld_api_key`:
+
+```
+workforce-analytics  wa_f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e5f6a7
+learning-development ld_b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9
+```
+
+**⚠️ Known wart:** the older outbound endpoints (`get-workforce-analytics.php`, and the four that serve
+other modules) were written before the convention settled and still validate the *L&D* key instead of
+the caller's. So today the pull needs `ld_…`, not `wa_…`. `get-workforce-integration-status.php`
+(the newest one) validates `wa_…` correctly. Use the keys above as-is; if L&D aligns the line, the pull
+switches to `wa_…` too and you will only change one constant.
+
+`ApiAuth` also accepts `Authorization: Bearer <key>` and, as a last resort, `?api_key=` — use the header.
+
+### Response contract you must handle
+
+| HTTP | Body | Meaning / what to do |
+|---|---|---|
+| 200 | `{"success":true,"message":"Received","id":41,"duplicate":false}` | Stored. Keep `id` for your own bookkeeping. |
+| 200 | `{"success":true,"message":"Already processed","duplicate":true}` | You re-sent a payload with an `external_reference_id` L&D already has. **Success** — do not retry differently. |
+| 400 | `{"success":false,"message":"Invalid JSON payload"}` | Body did not decode — fix your encoder. |
+| 401 | `{"success":false,"error":"Invalid API key"}` | Wrong key for that endpoint (see the table above) or `is_active = 0`. |
+| 405 | `{"success":false,"message":"Method not allowed"}` | You used GET on a POST endpoint. |
+| 422 | `{"success":false,"error":"department is required"}` | Validation. The message names the field — fix the payload, never blind-retry. |
+| 500 | `{"success":false,"error":"…"}` | L&D-side failure; it is logged in `ld_integration_log`. Retry twice with backoff. |
+
+Retry policy: retry **timeouts and 5xx** up to twice (1s, then 4s). Never retry 4xx. Resends are safe
+on the two tables that support `external_reference_id` (see below), so make retries idempotent by always
+sending the same reference.
+
+### `external_reference_id` — your idempotency handle
+
+- Supported by **training engagement** and **turnover risk** only. Send your own row id (e.g. `"12"`).
+- L&D stores `unique(source_module, external_reference_id)`, and separately records
+  `wa-engagement-<ref>` / `wa-turnover-<ref>` in `ld_integration_event` — so a retried POST returns
+  `duplicate:true` instead of creating a second row.
+- Keep it **stable across retries** and empty (or omitted) if you have no stable id.
+- **Competency and reporting requirements have no reference column** (their tables are shared with your
+  direct-write path and must stay byte-compatible). L&D cannot dedupe those for you: send each one once,
+  from a single place in your code, or keep your own "sent" marker.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Push: the four things L&D expects from you
+
+All four take the same shape: `POST`, JSON, `X-API-Key: wa_…`, optional `source_module` (defaults to
+`workforce`) and `created_by` (the employee id of the person who entered it — it shows up in L&D's
+audit trail and on their review page, so send it when you have a session).
+
+### 2.1 `receive-training-engagement.php` → `ld_training_engagement`
+
+| Field | Required | Values / defaults |
+|---|---|---|
+| `department` | ✅ | free text ≤150 |
+| `external_reference_id` | — | ≤120, unique per `source_module` (your idempotency key) |
+| `learner_team_type` | — | `individual-learner` (default) \| `department-team` \| `role-group` |
+| `learner_id` | — | int > 0 (the individual this is about) |
+| `learner_name` | — | ≤150 |
+| `training_activity` | — | `course` \| `learning-path` \| `workshop` \| `compliance-training` \| `other` (default `other` for anything unrecognised) |
+| `engagement_status` | — | `active` (default) \| `in-progress` \| `low` \| `inactive` |
+| `engagement_data` | — | text — the numbers behind your judgement |
+| `recommended_action` | — | text |
+| `notes` | — | text |
+
+Unknown enum values **fall back to the default** rather than failing, so a typo silently becomes
+`other`/`active`. Send the exact strings above.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST "$APP_URL/modules/learning/api/inbound/receive-training-engagement.php" \
+  -H "X-API-Key: wa_f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e5f6a7" \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "external_reference_id": "12",
+    "learner_team_type": "individual-learner",
+    "learner_id": 67999,
+    "learner_name": "David Aquino",
+    "department": "BTVTED",
+    "training_activity": "course",
+    "engagement_status": "low",
+    "engagement_data": "Only 1 of 4 required modules opened in 30 days; last access 26 days ago.",
+    "recommended_action": "Assign a refresher and check workload.",
+    "created_by": 7
+  }'
+```
+
+L&D review path: Learning → **Workforce Integration** (admin tabs) → status `received → monitoring → completed`.
+
+### 2.2 `receive-turnover-risk.php` → `ld_turnover_risk`
+
+| Field | Required | Values / defaults |
+|---|---|---|
+| `employee_id` **or** `employee_name` | ✅ (at least one) | int > 0 / ≤150 |
+| `external_reference_id` | — | ≤120, unique per `source_module` |
+| `department`, `position_name` | — | ≤150 each |
+| `risk_level` | — | `low` \| `medium` \| `high` \| `critical` (default `medium`) |
+| `risk_score` | — | 0–100, clamped, 2 decimals |
+| `risk_factors` | — | text — what drove the score |
+| `recommended_action` | — | text |
+| `assessment_date` | — | `YYYY-MM-DD` (or anything `strtotime()` reads) |
+
+**Use `critical` only when you mean it:** a `critical` risk_level pages the L&D team in-app the moment
+the record lands (`ld_notification`, type `workforce_alert`, audience = System Administrators +
+L&D Staff). It is deduped per record, so only the first insert alerts.
+
+L&D shows these next to the risk bands it computes itself (`ld_engagement_snapshot`, scored daily) and
+can turn one into a training request, which advances the record and notifies instructors.
+
+### 2.3 `receive-competency-requirement.php` → `ld_competency_requirement`
+
+| Field | Required | Values / defaults |
+|---|---|---|
+| `skill_name` | ✅ | ≤150 |
+| `target_department` | ✅ | ≤150 |
+| `target_proficiency` | ✅ | ≤50 (e.g. `Intermediate`) |
+| `expected_learning_output` | ✅ | ≤255 |
+| `employees_needing_training` | ✅ | int ≥ 0 |
