+## 6. Definition of done
+
+- [ ] A single helper (like §2.5) is the only thing that talks to L&D — no ad-hoc `file_get_contents` calls.
+- [ ] All four push paths send `external_reference_id` where the table supports it, stable across retries.
+- [ ] Another resend is a no-op (`duplicate:true`), not a duplicate row.
+- [ ] 401 / 422 / 5xx are distinguished in the UI; timeouts retry with backoff.
+- [ ] Exactly one writer per table — either the API or the direct `Employee::save*()` path (2.3/2.4).
+- [ ] The analytics pull runs on a schedule, is idempotent, and records its `snapshot_date`.
+- [ ] `wfa_skill_gap_analysis`, `wfa_risk_assessment`, `wfa_employee_metrics` are non-empty and refresh.
+- [ ] `critical` risk/competency records reach L&D's notifications, and the alert opens the
+      matching record (verified once) — see step 5.
+- [ ] Your pages show L&D's statuses from §4 for anything you sent.
